      "The placebo effect describes a genuine improvement in symptoms after receiving a treatment with no active therapeutic ingredient, simply because the patient believes it will work. Far from being an illusion confined to the mind, brain-imaging studies show that placebos can trigger measurable physiological changes, including the release of natural painkillers called endorphins.",
